.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH cadcraft-cli-convert 1  "convert " 
.SH NAME
cadcraft\-cli\-convert \- Convert a drawing; OUT\*(Aqs extension picks the format (dxf, dwg, dwt, svg, png, pdf)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcadcraft\-cli convert\fR [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-view\fR] [\fB\-\-in\-place\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-fontalt\fR] [\fB\-\-fontfallback\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIIN\fR> <\fIOUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert a drawing; OUT\*(Aqs extension picks the format (dxf, dwg, dwt, svg, png, pdf)
.PP
Image output (png 2400x1600, svg, pdf) shows model space, fitted to the drawing extents unless
\-\-window or \-\-view says otherwise.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<x0,y0,x1,y1>\fR
Show this rectangle (drawing units, x0<x1, y0<y1), centred and scaled to fit the image without distortion. A negative x0 needs the `=` form: \-\-window=\-10,0,10,5
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI<extents|current>\fR
What part of model space the image shows (case\-insensitive)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
extents: Always fit the drawing extents
.IP \(bu 2
current: The current view, as last set by zoom, pan or view.set (a freshly opened drawing\*(Aqs view is its extents plus a 10% margin)
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
Allow an output that is an input file, replacing the original
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIIN\fR>
The drawing to read (dxf, dwg, svg, svgz)
.TP
<\fIOUT\fR>
The file to write; its extension picks the format (dxf, dwg, dwt, svg, png, pdf)
.SH SETTINGS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
The settings folder; plotter configurations are in its `plotters` folder (default: the platform\*(Aqs settings folder). An empty value means no settings folder
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCADCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fontalt\fR \fI<FONT>\fR
The font that replaces a missing one (FONTALT)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCADCRAFT_FONTALT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-fontfallback\fR \fI<FONTS>\fR
The fonts tried, in order, for characters a font lacks, comma\-separated (FONTFALLBACK)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBCADCRAFT_FONTFALLBACK\fR environment variable. 
.RE
